# f1 = declared, f2 = callsAnother, f4 = throughAnArrow, f6 = once, f8 = run, f10 = filter, f11 = own, f18 = local
# A function that calls itself gets what loops get: what stands in its body runs again and again. That it calls itself is read off its own text: a declaration called by its name, a local function
# called by its binding, a function expression called by its own name, `this.run()` in run. There a method of lists that is handed a leaf made for the call is copied to the site, as inside a loop.
# NOT TAKEN: a method that calls its own name on another receiver (Heap.filter calls the list's filter) . two functions that call each other . a call of itself that stands in an arrow handed on .
# a function that does not call itself.
# RUN: walk f1 f2 f4 f6 f8 f10 f11 f18 mechanisms=all
# CHECK-LABEL: code f1:Body
# CHECK: frame 1 callee=
# CHECK: isLoopHead=true
# CHECK-LABEL: code f2:Body
# CHECK-NOT: isLoopHead=true
# CHECK-LABEL: code f4:Body
# CHECK-NOT: isLoopHead=true
# CHECK-LABEL: code f6:Body
# CHECK-NOT: isLoopHead=true
# CHECK-LABEL: code f8:Body
# CHECK: frame 1 callee=
# CHECK: isLoopHead=true
# CHECK-LABEL: code f10:Body
# CHECK-NOT: isLoopHead=true
# CHECK-LABEL: code f11:Body
# CHECK: frame 1 callee=
# CHECK: isLoopHead=true
# CHECK-LABEL: code f18:Body
# CHECK: frame 1 callee=
# CHECK: isLoopHead=true
# RUN(ANSWER): run-in-shell mechanisms=all
